  "id": "stimulus-onset-asynchrony",
  "term": "stimulus onset asynchrony",
  "definition": "Stimulus onset asynchrony (SOA) is the amount of delay between the onset of stimuli in a cognitive task. In this context, longer SOA means more time to prepare, which can change reaction time and task performance.",
